WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:11.898
Hi! Cap and cape differ by just one e, but they sound different. Today we'll learn letter patterns and long and short vowels, so spelling gets easier.

2
00:00:12.048 --> 00:00:16.914
Short vowels sound short: cap, pin, hop, cut.

3
00:00:17.064 --> 00:00:22.506
Add a silent e at the end and the vowel says its name: cape, pine.

4
00:00:22.656 --> 00:00:27.234
Ee and ea often make the long e sound: tree, sea.

5
00:00:27.384 --> 00:00:33.330
Ai comes in the middle of a word and ay at the end: rain, play.

6
00:00:33.480 --> 00:00:37.530
Sh makes the shh sound: ship, fish.

7
00:00:37.680 --> 00:00:40.818
Ch: chair, lunch.

8
00:00:40.968 --> 00:00:45.498
For th, put your tongue between your teeth: this, bath.

9
00:00:45.648 --> 00:00:52.530
After a short vowel, the k sound is often spelt ck: duck, sock.

10
00:00:52.680 --> 00:00:56.346
Watch out! Play doesn't end in ai!

11
00:00:56.496 --> 00:01:00.450
When the sound is at the end, write ay: play, day, say.

12
00:01:00.600 --> 00:01:05.874
In the middle of a word we write ai: rain, tail.

13
00:01:06.024 --> 00:01:15.282
Your turn! The, ___, is in the sky. Kite or kit? Pause and think.

14
00:01:15.432 --> 00:01:20.994
A kite has a silent e at the end. Did you get it right?

15
00:01:21.144 --> 00:01:30.642
Another one! I have a pet, ___. Which spelling is right? Pause and think.

16
00:01:30.792 --> 00:01:36.570
The shh sound is sh: fish. Did you get it right?

17
00:01:36.720 --> 00:01:46.242
Here's another! We sit on a, ___. Which spelling is right? Pause and think.

18
00:01:46.392 --> 00:01:51.618
Chair starts with ch. Did you get it right?

19
00:01:51.768 --> 00:02:01.458
Try one more! The, ___, says quack. Which spelling is right? Pause and think.

20
00:02:01.608 --> 00:02:07.698
After the short u, write ck: duck. Did you get it right?

21
00:02:07.848 --> 00:02:17.394
Try one more! I can see the, ___. Which spelling is right? Pause and think.

22
00:02:17.544 --> 00:02:23.418
Sea uses ea for the long e sound. Did you get it right?

23
00:02:23.568 --> 00:02:33.090
Try one more! It is a rainy, ___. Which spelling is right? Pause and think.

24
00:02:33.240 --> 00:02:38.874
At the end of the word, use ay: day. Did you get it right?

25
00:02:39.024 --> 00:02:48.738
Last one! Mum took a, ___, of me. Which spelling is right? Pause and think.

26
00:02:48.888 --> 00:02:55.002
In photo, the f sound is spelt ph. Did you get it right?

27
00:02:55.152 --> 00:03:03.642
Remember: a silent e makes the vowel long; ai goes in the middle and ay at the end; write ck after a short vowel.

28
00:03:03.792 --> 00:03:09.809
When you read today, look for words with sh, ch and th!

